WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.000
The host launches sixteen threads for

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.083
thirty-five elements. Block zero, thread

00:00:05.083 --> 00:00:07.583
three starts at global index three.

00:00:12.083 --> 00:00:14.464
The stride equals the total number of

00:00:14.464 --> 00:00:16.506
threads. Here, two blocks times eight

00:00:16.506 --> 00:00:18.547
threads gives a stride of sixteen.

00:00:23.047 --> 00:00:25.793
Starting at three, add sixteen for each

00:00:25.793 --> 00:00:28.147
visit. Which indices will this thread

00:00:28.147 --> 00:00:30.108
process before it reaches thirty-five?

00:00:38.608 --> 00:00:40.769
The thread visits indices three and

00:00:40.769 --> 00:00:42.930
nineteen. Thirty-five is outside the loop,

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.812
so it stops. At each visit, the thread

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.973
doubles the input into the output.
